{"id":"tuido-2203d3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Undo for delete, complete, and clear-all","description":"Destructive actions are one keystroke with no way back: `d` deletes immediately and `Space` toggles completion (which can hide the item when hide-completed is on). Only `X` has a confirmation.\n\nProposal: keep a small undo stack in `App` (src/app.rs) of snapshots or inverse operations for delete / toggle-complete / toggle-suspend / reorder / edit / reschedule / clear-all, bound to `u`. Show a hint in the Info panel after a destructive action (e.g. \"Deleted 'Call mom' — u to undo\"). Once undo exists, the X confirmation could optionally be dropped.\n\nAcceptance: deleting then pressing `u` restores the todo at its original position with the same id, and the restored state is saved to disk.","sort_order":"a0","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:02:12.313283Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"tuido-9cc989","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Richer natural-language due dates (weekdays, today, relative, absolute dates)","description":"src/schedule.rs only understands times of day (9pm, 21:30) plus the word \"tomorrow\". Common phrases are silently treated as plain text: \"Friday\", \"next Monday\", \"today\", \"tonight\", \"in 2 hours\", \"in 3 days\", \"Mar 14\", \"2026-11-01\".\n\nProposal: extend `parse_due_date` (which already takes an injected `now` for tests) to cover weekdays (next occurrence), today/tonight, `in N minutes|hours|days|weeks`, and absolute dates (ISO and \"Mon DD\"). Keep `clean_text` in sync so whatever is parsed is also stripped from the stored text — otherwise editing a todo re-triggers scheduling. Consider showing a live preview of the parsed due date in the input box title while typing.\n\nAcceptance: table-driven tests for each phrase; README's \"Adding Tasks with Due Dates\" section updated.","sort_order":"a1","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:02:12.344342Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"tuido-839e8f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Persist notification state so overdue reminders don't repeat on every launch","description":"`App::check_notifications` (src/app.rs) tracks already-notified todos in an in-memory `HashSet\u003cu32\u003e`. It's reset on every start, so each launch fires one desktop notification per overdue item — noisy with several stale overdue todos.\n\nProposal: persist a `notified_at: Option\u003cDateTime\u003cUtc\u003e\u003e` on `Todo` (src/model.rs, `#[serde(default)]` for backward compatibility with existing todos.json files). Notify only when `due_date \u003e notified_at` (or notified_at is None); clear it when the todo is rescheduled. Optionally add a periodic re-reminder interval.\n\nAcceptance: restarting the app with an already-notified overdue todo produces no new notification; rescheduling it produces exactly one when it next becomes due.","sort_order":"a2","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:02:12.374915Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"tuido-ae3d6f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Make suspended todos visually distinct","description":"Suspended todos are only marked by a `[~]` prefix in src/ui.rs (`todo_item`); they're otherwise styled like active items, while completed items are dimmed/crossed out and overdue ones are red. The scheduled ⏰ icon is still shown for suspended items even though they won't notify.\n\nProposal: render suspended items in a muted color (e.g. italic + yellow/dark-yellow, matching the Info panel's \"Status: Suspended\" color), drop or replace the ⏰ icon for them, and give the selected-suspended state its own highlight. Optionally add a toggle to hide suspended items alongside `h` for completed.","sort_order":"a3","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:02:12.407182Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"tuido-229065","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Respect XDG_CONFIG_HOME and allow a custom todo file path","description":"The todo file is hard-coded to `~/.config/tuido/todos.json` (src/storage.rs, `todos_path`). It ignores `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and there's no way to keep separate lists (work/personal) or point at a synced folder.\n\nProposal: resolve the path as: `--file \u003cpath\u003e` CLI flag \u003e `TUIDO_FILE` env var \u003e `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tuido/todos.json` \u003e `~/.config/tuido/todos.json`. `App` already receives the storage path as a parameter, so this only touches main.rs/storage.rs. Also add `--help` / `--version`. Document in README's Configuration section.\n\nAcceptance: existing users with ~/.config/tuido/todos.json see no change; each override works and is covered by a test of the resolution function.","sort_order":"a4","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:02:12.438393Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"tuido-97259f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"GitHub Actions CI and cross-platform release binaries","description":"There is no CI: nothing runs build/clippy/tests on push or PRs, and users can only install by building from source (README: `make install` / `cargo install --git`).\n\nAdd GitHub Actions workflows that (1) check every push/PR to main and (2) build prebuilt binaries for Linux, macOS, and Windows and publish them as release assets when a version tag is pushed. See spec for details.","sort_order":"a5","labels":["feature","infra"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:07:13.625873Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
